.TH WORKLOG 1 "2026" "worklog 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
worklog \- daily work journal with AI reports and PowerPoint export
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B worklog
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B worklog
keeps a plain-text journal, one file per day, one log entry per line.
Run it with no arguments to add today's logs interactively.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add [\-d DATE] [TEXT...]
Add entries. With TEXT, adds one entry; without, prompts line by line (empty line to finish).
DATE may be YYYY\-MM\-DD, DD\-MM\-YYYY, today, yesterday, or an offset such as \-2.
.TP
.B view [\-d DATE] | [\-y [YEAR]] [\-\-summary]
Show the entries of a day, or with \-y a whole year grouped by month (YEAR: this, last, YYYY).
\-\-summary with \-y prints only the monthly totals.
.TP
.B year [PERIOD] [\-\-summary] [\-\-report | \-\-ppt] [\-\-no\-ai] [\-o FILE]
Shortcut for the year view (PERIOD: this, last, YYYY; default this). \-\-report also writes the
yearly AI report, and \-\-ppt also builds the yearly deck (\-\-no\-ai skips the API call).
.TP
.B edit [\-d DATE]
Edit a day in $VISUAL / $EDITOR.
.TP
.B calendar [YYYY\-MM]
Interactive month calendar. Arrow keys move, n/p change month, Enter views a day,
e edits it, a adds entries, t jumps to today, q quits. Days with entries are marked with *.
.TP
.B report weekly|monthly|yearly [\-p PERIOD] [\-o FILE]
Generate a detailed AI report in Markdown. PERIOD is this, last, YYYY\-Www (weekly),
YYYY\-MM (monthly) or YYYY (yearly). Without \-o the report is saved under the data directory.
.TP
.B ppt weekly|monthly|yearly [\-p PERIOD] [\-o FILE] [\-\-no\-ai]
Create a PowerPoint (.pptx) deck. Needs python3\-pptx. With \-\-no\-ai the slides are built
directly from the logs and no API call is made.
.TP
.B config show|set KEY VALUE|path
Keys: provider (anthropic or openai), model, api_key, base_url, max_tokens.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WORKLOG_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY
API key; overrides the key stored in the config file.
.TP
.B WORKLOG_HOME
Store data and config in this directory instead of the XDG locations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/worklog/logs/YYYY/YYYY\-MM\-DD.txt
The daily logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/worklog/config.json
Settings (mode 600).
.SH NOTES
Reports and AI-built slides send the relevant log text to the configured AI provider.
